export anchor NightPaperStyle:
    number: 323
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Night paper
    idea: The monitor typeset as a short evening report on warm dark grey paper, a serif reading column with a summary headline, inline sparklines in the prose, a leader dotted service list, numbered figures, and alerts and deploys as margin notes.
    base: dark
    palette:
        paper: #29251f, the page and every surface including the style sheet
        paperShade: #322d26, a rare tint kept for hover
        ink: #ebe2d2, text, the request line, p50 and the primary button
        pencil: #bcb09b, captions, times and small caps labels
        rule: #4d463c, hairlines, double rules, dot leaders and the chart grid
        rust: #e6a873, links, the dashed p95 line, the incident label, the secondary button and focus
        healthy: #acd6a2, Healthy and Resolved with outline circle and square
        degraded: #ecc47c, Degraded and Investigating with outline triangle and magnifier
        recovered: #adc9ea, Recovered with an outline diamond
        firing: #f2a89d, Firing with an outline octagon and the error line
    type:
        Charter, Bitstream Charter, Iowan Old Style, Sitka Text, Cambria,
        Georgia. Base 18px at 1.65. The headline is 40px at 400 and 1.15,
        the lead 20px, section labels 15px small caps tracked 0.14em in
        pencil, captions 15px italic, numbers old style.
    layout:
        A 1080px page with a 680px reading column and a 260px margin column
        56px apart. A masthead with Brightwork Ops in small caps, an italic
        Production the last twenty four hours, and the suite apps as small
        text links joined by middots with Ops underlined in rust, all over a
        hairline. The headline reads A steady day, one open incident on
        sync-worker. The lead paragraph gives the traffic range with a small
        inline sparkline and the error spike with a red sparkline, notes the
        billing outage, and names the degraded service and INC-0427. A
        Services section lists each service in italic with a dotted leader
        to its status shape, word and uptime, and a smaller note line for
        p95, queue depth or recovery. The open incident sits between double
        rules with a rust small caps label, the ID at 26px, a sentence of
        facts and Investigating, then Open the incident and Read the
        runbook. Figures holds a wide Figure 1 for requests and two smaller
        Figures 2 and 3 for error rate and latency, each with an italic
        caption. The margin column carries Alerts and Deploys as notes with
        italic times. Below 1000px margin notes drop under the article.
    spacing: An 8px unit. A 680px column, a 56px gutter, a 260px margin column, and 32 to 40px between sections.
    density: Low. One reading column where facts arrive as sentences, a short list and three figures.
    corners: None. Only the swatches are round.
    borders: Hairline rules above sections, a double rule around the incident and dotted leaders in the service list.
    shadows: None. The paper is flat.
    icons:
        Almost none. Small outline status shapes sit inline before the
        word, circle, triangle, diamond, octagon, square and magnifier.
        Sparklines sit in the prose.
    focus: A 2px dotted rust outline offset 4px with a faint warm wash.
    tone: Plain sentences such as A steady day, one open incident on sync-worker, and Read the runbook.
